---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: eprfs-core-tree-boundary
purpose: >
  Artifact-neutral addressing and filesystem tree contracts. The planned shared tree is an
  immutable, versioned content-addressed value; local projection state remains rebuildable.
rules:
  - id: immutable-tree-is-not-projection-manifest
    class: inject
    when:
      write: "*.rs"
      contains-any: ["TreeNode", "TreeEntry", "ProjectionManifest", "ProjectionEntry"]
    dedupe-of: "elohim/eprfs/eprfs-core/src/projection.rs (existing mutable local view)"
    why: >
      Place the planned canonical tree/address types in eprfs-core as immutable,
      versioned, artifact-neutral values: byte names, raw leaves, modes, symlink target
      bytes, explicit external boundaries and build closure. ProjectionManifest and
      ProjectionEntry in projection.rs describe a mutable local view with adapter
      metadata; ProjectionAwareness carries local status. Neither is the canonical
      source or a tree CID. Git submodule pins, OIDs,
      index and worktree interpretation belong in brit's Git bridge; build recipes and
      hApp/Cargo packaging belong in rakia adapters. Migrate brit's BritCid
      through eprfs-core's explicit tag-42 BlobLink only with byte/CID conformance;
      a direct BlobCid alias can change serialized bytes. Preserve EprMeta v1 bytes.
---

# eprfs-core — portable tree contract

`address.rs` provides codec-aware `BlobCid` addressing and the explicit `BlobLink` wire
wrapper (tag-42 in DAG-CBOR, strings in JSON); existing `BlobCid` serialization is unchanged.
The wrapper is additive: consumers and registry versions have not migrated.
`projection.rs` describes local projection entries. The immutable shared tree in the approved native developer
through-line is planned work, not an existing `ProjectionManifest` capability. Its bytes
must be stable across artifact adapters. A CID proves bytes, not publication standing or
which release head was elected; those decisions remain with content governance.
